(2 panels + 3 states + 27 strings).

=== REASONING ===
- Mirrored the established surface convention (NotificationChannelsView / DestinationETAWidget):
  pure Adapter (decode/projection/i18n) + @Observable Model + Source seam + InMemory source for
  previews/tests + a Shared-backed Live source (the single Shared-touching type) + Previews + Tests.
- Reads bind via the verified StateHolderModel(flow:transform:) + LoadableState.from pattern
  (identical to BatteryRadialGauge/DestinationETA), decoding the Resource<JsonElement> array through
  String(describing:)→JSONSerialization (the DestinationETA precedent). Empty array → .loaded([]) →
  empty phase (web safeArray parity).
- Mutations call AdminStore.createApiKey/deleteApiKey/revokeApiKey; the created-secret is extracted
  from the response object (web data.key). The exact bridged shape of the Kotlin Result-returning
  suspend funcs is pinned on the macOS Xcode build against Shared.xcframework (ADR-004), the same
  convention FacadeError/FlowBridge document for unverifiable Shared symbols.
- Strings resolve from the platform catalog (Localizable.xcstrings) via LocalizedStringKey /
  String(localized:) (ADR-014); keys are the verbatim web t() phrases. Delete-confirm keeps the
  verbatim "{{name}}" token and substitutes at the display boundary.
- 3 data states implemented (loading skeletons / empty ContentUnavailableView / success staggered
  list); an additional error+Retry arm is included (ADR-011: never a blank region). Permission badge
  uses token colours (read→statusSuccess, read-write→statusWarning, admin→chartSeriesPower purple),
  no raw hex. Adaptive: toolbar primaryAction on macOS/iOS, list reflows; ≥44pt targets, VoiceOver
  labels, Dynamic Type, light/dark/high-contrast via tokens.
- Navigation: added AppRoute.apiKeys (system group, /api-keys deep link via AppRouteParser) +
  APIKeysRouteRegistration (mirrors SettingsRouteRegistration). TeslaSyncApp composes the route
  registry; the live SharedAPIKeysSource activates once AppContainer bootstraps the AdminStore
  (deferred app-wide, like every other shared-backed route).

